  "response": "```python\ndef merg_intervals(intervals):\n▁▁▁▁\"\"\"\n▁▁▁▁Merge overlapping or touching closed intervals without mutating input; return sorted intervals.\n\n▁▁▁▁Args:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁intervals (list of list of int): A list of closed intervals, where each interval is a list of two integers [start, end].\n\n▁▁▁▁Returns:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁list of list of int: A list of merged and sorted closed intervals.\n▁▁▁▁\"\"\"\n\n▁▁▁▁if not intervals:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁return []\n\n▁▁▁▁# Sort the intervals based on their start values\n▁▁▁▁intervals = sorted(intervals, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n▁▁▁▁merged_intervals = []\n▁▁▁▁current_interval = intervals[0]\n\n▁▁▁▁for i in range(1, len(intervals)):\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁next_interval = intervals[i]\n\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁# Check for overlap or touching\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁if next_interval[0] <= current_interval[1]:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁# Merge the intervals\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁current_interval[1] = max(current_interval[1], next_interval[1])\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁else:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁# No overlap, add the current interval to the merged list and start a new one\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁merged_intervals.append(current_interval)\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁current_interval = next_interval\n\n▁▁▁▁# Add the last interval to the merged list\n▁▁▁▁merged_intervals.append(current_interval)\n\n▁▁▁▁return merged_intervals\n```",
